# One hand-written case per topic: (situation, model answer). Teaching cases, invented people-free, figures in reais.
CASES = {
"Internet Companies": ("A new online shop for school supplies in Sao Paulo gets 3,000 visits a week but only 24 orders. Most visitors leave at the payment page on phones.", "Test the payment page on a mid-range phone, add PIX with a one-tap code, show delivery cost before checkout, and measure again for two weeks. Target: orders from 24 to at least 45 a week."),
"IT": ("A 12-person accounting office loses a day of work when its file server fails; there was a backup, but no one has ever restored it.", "Run a restore drill, move files to a cloud share with versioning, write a 15-minute outage runbook, and offer a monthly plan with a written response time. Evidence: a timed restore log."),
"Health": ("A neighbourhood wellness centre advertises a 'cure' for back pain after three good client stories.", "Remove the cure claim, describe the service honestly as a programme to reduce pain and improve movement, record outcomes with a standard score before and after, and refer red-flag symptoms to a doctor."),
"Real Estate": ("A buyer loves a flat priced R$ 480.000, but the seller cannot show the latest condominium debt statement.", "Pause the offer, request the registry certificate, tax and condominium clearance in writing, and agree who pays any debt. Only sign when the file is clean."),
"Food": ("A small bakery wants to sell packaged cakes to cafes. One cafe asks about allergens and shelf life; the owner has no answer.", "Write the recipe with allergens, test shelf life at set storage, label batch and expiry, and keep a batch record that traces flour lots. Then offer the cafe a sample with the label."),
"Energy": ("A shop owner wants a larger solar system than the roof and the main breaker can support.", "Survey the roof and the supply, size the system to the safe limit, explain the grid approval steps, and quote a smaller design with an upgrade option."),
"Oil & Gas": ("A contractor crew wants to start a welding task near a fuel line before the permit is signed because the client is waiting.", "Stop. Use the stop-work right, complete the gas test and permit, brief the crew, and then start. A late start is cheaper than a fire."),
"Telecom": ("A neighbourhood with 400 homes reports weak service every evening. A new link would cost R$ 60.000.", "Measure evening load for a week, check whether the problem is the backhaul or the last mile, and fix the cheapest bottleneck first. Show the subscriber the speed test before and after."),
"Smart Home Builder": ("A family wants every light on a phone app, but grandparents do not use phones.", "Keep wall switches working, add a simple wall panel, test scenes with the grandparents present, and hand over a one-page guide."),
"Road & Bridge Development": ("Heavy rain during sub-base work leaves one section soft; the schedule is tight.", "Stop the next layer, test density and moisture, remove or dry the soft material, record the fix, and tell the owner the revised date."),
"Automated Farming Equipment": ("A cooperative tries a seeding machine, but half the members worry about breakdown during planting week.", "Offer a shared spare-parts kit, train two operators per farm, schedule a pre-season service, and measure cost per hectare against hand labour."),
"Construction Safety Management": ("An audit finds three workers on a roof edge with no fall protection, but the foreman says it is only a ten-minute job.", "Stop the task, fit guardrails or harnesses with anchor points, record the finding with an owner and date, and retrain the crew. The ten-minute excuse is exactly how falls happen."),
"Sensor Manufacture": ("A buyer reports that one batch of temperature sensors drifts 1.5 degrees after six months.", "Trace the batch record, recalibrate samples, find the cause (for example a changed adhesive), quarantine remaining stock, and inform the buyer with a fix date."),
"Internet Infrastructure": ("A power cut lasts 40 minutes and the backup generator fails to start.", "Restore from battery, log the failure, replace the starter, add a monthly start-under-load test, and tell clients the cause and the new test schedule."),
"International Trade": ("A buyer abroad asks for a quote on 2,000 cartons; customs says your product code does not match the one on the invoice.", "Correct the classification with the customs broker before shipping, update the invoice, check duties and licences, and only then confirm the delivery date."),
"Tourist Automation": ("A booking tool shows a museum open on Monday when it is closed, and several visitors arrive to a locked door.", "Fix the listing, refund affected bookings, add a daily check with the museum, and display 'last confirmed' on every listing."),
"Online / AI Investment Management": ("A young saver wants high returns in six months and is not willing to lose anything.", "Explain that high return needs risk, record the goal and loss limit, propose an emergency fund and a low-risk mix, and decline to promise returns."),
"Universities": ("Employers say graduates can discuss theory but cannot prepare a simple budget.", "Rewrite one module around the task 'prepare a departmental budget', add a project with a real employer brief, assess with a rubric, and track graduate outcomes."),
"Technical & Vocational Schools": ("A welding course has 30 learners and four booths.", "Rotate learners through booths in small groups, add simulation and theory when idle, assess each on a task, and plan equipment maintenance."),
"Sustainability Management": ("A factory claims it cut energy use by 30%, but cannot show the baseline.", "Rebuild the baseline from last year's bills, normalise for output, verify the saving, and publish only the verified figure."),
"Drones": ("A client wants a roof inspection next to a school during break time.", "Decline the time slot, check airspace and local rules, schedule outside school hours with ground control and signage, and keep the aircraft away from people."),
"Distribution Companies": ("Three shops complain of short deliveries within a week.", "Check pick lists and loading counts, add a count at loading and at delivery with sign-off, and trace the cause to a stage."),
"Package Delivery Services": ("One zone shows 18% failed deliveries because recipients are out.", "Offer delivery windows, message the recipient before arrival, add a neighbour or locker option, and measure failed attempts weekly."),
"Renewable Energy for Homes, Offices, Malls, Multiplexes": ("A multiplex wants solar on a roof that is shaded for part of the day.", "Run a shade analysis, size only the unshaded area, estimate generation as a range, and propose a monitoring plan."),
"Sports": ("A youth coach pushes 12-year-olds to train daily, and two report knee pain.", "Reduce load, include rest days, ask a qualified professional about the pain, and set an age-appropriate programme."),
"Brand Management": ("A coffee shop advertises 'fastest service in town' but queues are long at peak hours.", "Change the promise to one the operation can keep (for example 'ready in 5 minutes or free'), test it for two weeks, and fix the peak-hour process."),
"Travel Agencies": ("A group of 20 travellers learn on the day that a hotel cancelled their booking.", "Move them to an equal or better hotel at the agency's cost, communicate immediately, claim from the supplier, and add a 48-hour reconfirmation step."),
"Microgreens Farming": ("White fuzz appears on one rack of radish trays.", "Separate the rack, identify mould versus root hairs, check airflow and watering, sanitise trays, change seed lot if needed, and log the cause."),
"Care for Disabled and Elderly People": ("An elderly client falls in the bathroom while a carer is in the next room.", "Give first aid and call help, record the incident, review the bathroom (grab rails, mat, lighting), update the care plan, and inform the family."),
"Private Medicare": ("A clinic receives repeated claim denials from one health plan.", "Audit codes and documents for the denied claims, find the common error, retrain billing staff, and track the denial rate monthly."),
"Home Security and Monitoring Services": ("A customer has three false alarms in a week from a pet.", "Adjust the sensor type or position, test again, check alarm verification steps, and explain the change to the customer."),
"Language Schools": ("Adult learners keep leaving after the third week.", "Interview those who left, shorten the cycle, add speaking tasks tied to their jobs, and follow up on absences within one day."),
"Courses for Foreigners": ("New workers need Portuguese for the clinic but the class teaches football words.", "Replace the scenario with clinic dialogues, practise with role-plays, add vocabulary cards, and test with a real phone call."),
"Construction and Technical Services": ("A client asks to add a bathroom to a job that is half done.", "Write a change order with scope, time and price, get written approval, and only then proceed."),
"Winery": ("A batch of wine tastes of vinegar a week before bottling.", "Isolate the tank, test acidity, trace the oxygen or hygiene failure, decide to treat or discard, and tighten cleaning logs."),
"Export and Import Business": ("A shipment of handmade goods is held at the port because the packing list does not match the invoice.", "Correct documents through the broker, pay storage fees under agreement, and add a document check before dispatch."),
"Financing Start-ups": ("A founder asks for R$ 200.000 with a polished pitch but no paying customers.", "Offer a smaller first tranche tied to milestones such as ten paying customers, and review in 90 days."),
"Food Trucking": ("Rain halves the evening trade, and the truck has stock left.", "Plan weather-based prep, freeze or reuse safe items, add pre-orders, and review daily waste."),
"Bed and Breakfast Business": ("A guest posts a poor review about noise from the street.", "Reply politely, offer an earplug kit and a quiet room option, and update the listing."),
"Hostel or Hotel Business": ("A group arrives early but rooms are not ready.", "Offer luggage storage and a breakfast, prioritise those rooms, and improve the housekeeping order."),
"Carpentry": ("A client dislikes the colour of a finished table.", "Compare with the signed sample, offer to refinish at cost if different, and use a sample board in future."),
"Event Organization and Management": ("A sudden storm threatens an outdoor wedding for 150 guests.", "Switch to the indoor backup, brief suppliers, announce, and tidy the timeline."),
"Franchise Business": ("A franchisee changes the recipe to save cost.", "Audit with the scorecard, explain the brand risk, require a return to the standard, and apply the agreement."),
"Manufacturing Business": ("A buyer rejects 8% of a batch for size tolerance.", "Check gauge calibration, trace to a tool wear, add in-process checks, and sort or rework."),
"Apparels and Accessories": ("Customers return many trousers for poor fit.", "Check the size chart against measurements, adjust the pattern, add fit notes, and track returns."),
"Beauty": ("A client reports a rash after a hair colour.", "Stop use, advise medical help, record product and batch, review patch-test routine, and report to the supplier."),
"Dental": ("An autoclave log shows a missed cycle for one set of instruments.", "Quarantine the set, re-sterilise, review the log, and retrain."),
"Cleaning Services": ("A cleaner mixes two products and gets a headache.", "Ventilate, give first aid, stop mixing, label products, and retrain on safe dilution."),
"Warehousing and Storage Services": ("A cycle count shows 12 pallets missing from the system.", "Search locations, review movement logs, correct the system, and put put-away checks in place."),
"Transportation and Courier Services": ("A driver reports a tyre problem but wants to finish the route.", "Stop for safety, replace the tyre, notify customers, and add a pre-trip check."),
"3D Printing Business": ("Prints fail at 70% of height.", "Check temperature, bed, and filament, run a test, and record settings."),
"App Development": ("Users abandon the sign-up screen.", "Watch five sessions, shorten the form, test, and measure completion."),
"Small and Medium Entrepreneur Business": ("A shop owner sells well but is always out of cash.", "Build the 13-week cash plan, chase late payers, and delay a non-urgent purchase."),
"Outsourcing Services": ("A client complains about errors in monthly reports.", "Find the stage where errors enter, add double check, retrain, and report weekly to the client."),
"Electronics Sales & Repair Services": ("A customer complains that a repaired phone lost photos.", "Explain the backup policy, recover if possible, add a consent form, and offer a backup step."),
}
